==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] (600%) spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 22.67~25.33 seconds<sup>680f~760f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Those Guys]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**30 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 6.67~9.33 seconds<sup>200f~280f</sup>.
**20 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 18.67~24 seconds<sup>560f~720f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns.
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns.

==Strategy==
For the most part, this stage is perfectly manageable with just a generalist loadout. Bring 4-5 meatshields, preferably strong ones; and cheap ranged attackers such as ([[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] variants, etc.) are recommended, but more expensive units such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] can also be brought, as killing the peons give quite a bit of money.

At the beginning, just spawn a few meatshields and ranged attackers to stall. Killing the Celeboodles should be easy, and they will give you decent money. After hitting the enemy base, Teacher Bun Bun and Dark Emperor Nyandam will spawn. Spam meatshields, your ranged attackers, and Bun Bun will go down soon enough. After Bun Bun is dead, Dark Emperor Nyandam should die easily, and that will be the end of it.

==Trivia==
*Since it drops [[Catamin]]s, which look like bottles of Lipovitan D (a stronger version of the energy drink [[wikipedia:Lipovitan|Lipovitan]]), The Precipice is likely a reference to a [https://youtu.be/MdpkqbrMUAo famous Lipovitan D commercial] which depicts two mountaineers struggling to climb a precipice.

